{
 "about": "10CL016 PLL_1 counters (offline; xdev pll:, pllc:, pll5: designs, altpll from the 48 MHz pin E2). All PLL bits are in periphery logical frame 0, plane 1 (periph.py); no core bits change. Seven counters, one 18-byte block each at base b: hi = 8 bits at b..b+7, odd flag at b+8 (set iff hi != lo), lo = 8 bits at b+9..b+16, bypass flag at b+17 (count = 1). count = hi + lo. Bases: N 193, M 175, C0 157, C1 139, C2 121, C3 103, C4 85. f_VCO = 48 MHz * M / N, f_Ck = f_VCO / Ck. Reproduces all 46 single-output builds and, as a set, the five outputs of 3 five-output builds (Quartus chooses which physical counter serves which clk port). Bytes 219..224 change with M/N (loop-filter / charge-pump, not decoded). Earlier notes called byte 174 an 'M flag'; it is C0's bypass flag.",
